From 620dd5c61bf4ba9454a060595f52d6e2c63242bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 17:18:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] package the vendored MediaInfoLib and ZenLib licences

Upstream's own Linux wheels bundle a prebuilt libmediainfo.so.0 fetched from
mediaarea.net, which publishes no riscv64 build; this port compiles it from
the MediaInfoLib and ZenLib sources instead (both BSD/zlib-licensed), so the
wheel needs their licence text alongside pymediainfo's own MIT one.

`[project.license] text = "MIT"` is the legacy table form, which pdm-backend
only expands into the default `LICEN[CS]E*`/`COPYING*`/`NOTICE*` glob when no
`license-files` is set at all. Move to the PEP 639 SPDX string and add an
explicit `license-files` list covering both the existing LICENSE and the two
new vendored licence texts; PEP 639 then requires dropping the now-redundant
`License ::` classifier.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [only relevant to this port's riscv64 build, which compiles the library upstream's own wheels fetch prebuilt]
---
 licenses/mediainfolib.txt | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 licenses/zenlib.txt       | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 pyproject.toml            |  5 ++---
 3 files changed, 44 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 licenses/mediainfolib.txt
 create mode 100644 licenses/zenlib.txt

diff --git a/licenses/mediainfolib.txt b/licenses/mediainfolib.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4169054
--- /dev/null
+++ b/licenses/mediainfolib.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
